00:42:59.610 --> 00:43:19.370
<v Sean Cole>It's This American Life. I'm Sean Cole. Every week we choose a theme and play you all kinds of stories related to that theme. This week, "Who Do We Think We Are?", stories of folks trying to reconcile their beliefs with those of someone or someones they're related to. We're up to Act Two of the show. Act Two, "Who Wants to Know?"
<v Sean Cole>接下来，一对姐弟，名字极其相似，却用完全相反的方式应对小时候父亲遭遇的变故。一分钟后，当我们的节目继续，来自芝加哥WBEZ。

00:43:19.370 --> 00:43:44.380
<v Sean Cole>This last story is also about folks coming to a kind of reckoning with their parents, but in a very different way. It's about a brother and sister named Nema and Neda Semnani. Their father died violently when they were very little. Nema, the brother, actually never met his father, and their mother died of ovarian cancer back in 2010. After she died, they packed up boxes and boxes of her stuff and sent them off with various relatives.
<v Sean Cole>这里是《美国生活》。我是肖恩·科尔。每周我们选择一个主题，并为你播放与主题相关的所有故事。本周是“我们是谁？”，讲述人们试图调和自己的信仰与亲人之间差异的故事。我们现在进行到节目的第二幕。第二幕，“谁想知道？”

00:43:44.380 --> 00:43:59.350
<v Sean Cole>Nema ended up with a bunch of the boxes himself, and a filing cabinet, which he hated. He didn't want to look at any of it. Both of his parents were dead. There was history in there that he didn't want to deal with. And he was moving around a lot, apartment to apartment.
<v Sean Cole>这个故事也是关于人们与父母达成某种和解，但方式非常不同。故事主角是姐弟俩：内马·塞姆纳尼和内达·塞姆纳尼。他们的父亲在他们很小的时候惨死。身为弟弟的内马甚至没见过父亲，而母亲于2010年死于卵巢癌。母亲去世后，他们装好一箱又一箱她的遗物，并让亲戚们带走。

00:43:59.350 --> 00:44:12.890
<v Nema Semnani>Imagine lugging around a both literal and figurative box of just bad with you, like figuratively full of bad stuff and physically a lot of it. You know?
<v Nema Semnani>内马自己留下了一堆箱子和一个他讨厌的文件柜。他不想看里面的任何东西。他的父母都去世了。那里藏着他不想面对的历史。而且他搬家很频繁，公寓换了一个又一个。

